+# Test plan — entry 1 (rotated segment)
+
+Rotated from `test-plan.md` at entry 2's strategy pass (`artifact-layout.md` "Test plan" rotation). A cross-span reader reads this segment in ordinal order, then the live file.
+
+## Risk → check decisions
+
+Impacted set, entry 1: the **full suite**. The shared-infrastructure safety valve (`sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impacted test set") fires, because the change surface touches `.asd/sync.js` (the generator behind every provider view), `core.md` (the rule hub every agent loads) and `release-manifest.json`. `tests/run.js` is one flat file with no selector (`commands.yaml` sets no `test_affected`), so a scoped run would also have to filter by name.
+
+Every check below is static or unit level inside `tests/run.js`, following the file's existing content-contract pattern. None of them needs new infrastructure or a new dependency.
